n the source supports them; one reading plus explicit unresolved questions is acceptable. A formalization describes a named selected control, not whole-bank compliance. Keep fact names, types and definitions stable across comparable alternatives. Formal expressions use parenthesized prefix notation, never Java or Python:\ntrue, false, a declared fact name; (integer 6), (money_hkd 100), (date 2024-11-30);\n(and EXPR EXPR ...), (or EXPR EXPR ...), (not EXPR), (if CONDITION THEN ELSE),\n(= LEFT RIGHT), (> LEFT RIGHT), (>= LEFT RIGHT), (+ LEFT RIGHT), (- LEFT RIGHT).\nDates are Gregorian YYYY-MM-DD, numeric literals are exact integer strings.\nUse the same type on both sides of a comparison. Unknown facts remain unknown.\nscope is Boolean; result has result_type. Never invent a fact's truth value.\nUse null formalization if a requirement cannot be represented in this fragment.\nEvery declared fact needs a meaningful definition, units, source refs and an\nexplicit indication of whether supplying it requires professional judgment. Declare the actual question answered by the result. For Boolean compliance or prohibition decisions begin statement with [TRUE_IS_COMPLIANT] or [TRUE_IS_PROHIBITED] respectively. For a Boolean condition, trigger or eligibility predicate use [TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] and explain precisely what true and false mean. Never relabel a licensing trigger as compliance, prohibition or licence possession. For non-Boolean results use [VALUE] and state the units. These meanings are proposals, not approvals.","method":"Investigate the selected parent using the requested move, uncited source units and supplied counterexamples. Retain justified rival readings and explain any failed hypothesis.","move":"exception-attachment","parent":{"assumptions":["This reading models the announced exemption's applicability, conditional on classification under the referenced margin regime; it does not determine the circular's independent legal force.","The stated commencement date is inclusive. Amendment and gazettal are treated as pending implementation steps because the supplied text does not expressly condition commencement on them.","Overseas monitoring, reporting and duration provisions are explanatory background rather than incorporated SFC requirements.","The absence of a supplied later notice does not establish that no relevant later notice exists."],"citations":[{"quote":"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) issues this circular to inform licensed corporations that it will exempt non-centrally cleared single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options (collectively, “non-centrally cleared equity options”) from its margin requirements1 from 4 January 2026 until further notice to align with the latest global developments.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u0.0"},{"quote":"considering that licensed corporations’ exposures to non-centrally cleared equity options are currently insignificant","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u1.381"},{"quote":"In the EU, a permanent exemption from the requirement to exchange margin for single-stock equity options and equity index options became effective on 24 December 2024, subject to monitoring and periodic reporting2.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u3.801"},{"quote":"It implemented an indefinite exemption from the UK bilateral margining requirements for single-stock equity options and index options.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u4.1019"},{"quote":"Paragraph 7(e) of Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct will be amended accordingly and gazetted in due course.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357"},{"quote":"1 As set out in Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671"}],"distinction":"This reading gives the announcement its stated commencement and temporary duration while preserving the missing legal implementation question. Requiring completed gazettal, importing EU reporting conditions, imposing an exposure threshold or treating the exemption as permanent would materially change eligibility, but the supplied text does not sufficiently support those as competing operative readings.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"Whether the selected actor is a licensed corporation for purposes of this SFC announcement at the assessment date.","name":"actor_is_licensed_corporation","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the selected transaction and margin requirement fall within the referenced Part III of Schedule 10 margin regime apart from the announced equity-options exemption, including underlying actor classifications and other applicable scope limits.","name":"within_referenced_margin_regime","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0","d802c45a4262c.u15.1671"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the selected transaction is a single-stock option, equity basket option or equity index option.","name":"is_listed_equity_option","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"Whether the selected option is non-centrally cleared at the assessment date.","name":"is_non_centrally_cleared","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"},{"meaning":"The date for which the selected exemption-applicability control is evaluated.","name":"assessment_date","requires_judgment":false,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"date","unit":"Gregorian calendar date"},{"meaning":"Whether a further SFC notice effective by the assessment date has ended or superseded reliance on this announced exemption for the selected actor, transaction and margin requirement. A true value does not decide eligibility under any replacement exemption.","name":"further_notice_displaces_announced_exemption","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["d802c45a4262c.u0.0"],"type":"bool","unit":"Boolean"}],"result":"(and is_listed_equity_option is_non_centrally_cleared (>= assessment_date (date 2026-01-04)) (not further_notice_displaces_announced_exemption))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and actor_is_licensed_corporation within_referenced_margin_regime)"},"local_id":"r1","questions":["Does the missing Code text qualify which licensed corporations or margin obligations can use the announced exemption?","What legal effect does pending amendment and gazettal have beyond the announcement's stated commencement?","What later-notice evidence is available for the selected assessment date?"],"statement":"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] Selected control: applicability of the announced SFC equity-options margin exemption. Within the declared actor and underlying margin-regime scope, true means the selected transaction is a listed non-centrally cleared equity option, the assessment date is on or after 2026-01-04, and no effective further notice has displaced reliance on this announcement for it. False means at least one of those conditions fails; it does not establish a margin breach or exclude another exemption. Outside scope this control makes no determination. Unknown inputs remain unknown.","subject":"Announced exemption for a selected licensed corporation, option transaction, margin requirement and assessment date"},"protocol":"legalmath.search.v1","role":"adversarial-investigator","source_packet":{"authority":"RETAINED_SOURCE","dependencies":[{"dependency_id":"missing.60583204ae3dc30d17bad37f","source_hash":null},{"dependency_id":"missing.3fa08e37cc9ca8964c94abb9","source_hash":null},{"dependency_id":"missing.4dd72c04a8ea00444bb6b1a9","source_hash":null}],"family_ids":["scope","definitions","exceptions","modality","time","dependencies"],"selected_slice":"Applicability of the announced SFC margin exemption from 4 January 2026 for classified licensed corporations and non-centrally cleared single-stock, equity-basket or equity-index options. Preserve until-further-notice temporal limitation, pending Code amendment, and the distinction between SFC operative scope and overseas explanatory background.","source_key":"assurance.387982acc9842136e9fa9d1e","units":[{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u0.0","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"The Securities and Futures Commission (SFC) issues this circular to inform licensed corporations that it will exempt non-centrally cleared single-stock options, equity basket options and equity index options (collectively, “non-centrally cleared equity options”) from its margin requirements1 from 4 January 2026 until further notice to align with the latest global developments.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u0.0"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u1.381","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"The margin requirements for non-centrally cleared equity options were originally scheduled to take effect on that date. However, to prevent regulatory arbitrage and considering that licensed corporations’ exposures to non-centrally cleared equity options are currently insignificant, the SFC has decided to align the exemptions of its margin requirements with the approaches in the European Union (EU) and the UK:","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u1.381"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u3.801","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"In the EU, a permanent exemption from the requirement to exchange margin for single-stock equity options and equity index options became effective on 24 December 2024, subject to monitoring and periodic reporting2.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u3.801"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u4.1019","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"On 27 November 2025, the UK’s Prudential Regulation Authority and Financial Conduct Authority published a joint policy statement3 containing amendments to the Binding Technical Standards 2016/22514. It implemented an indefinite exemption from the UK bilateral margining requirements for single-stock equity options and index options.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u4.1019"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Paragraph 7(e) of Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct will be amended accordingly and gazetted in due course.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u7.1479","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Should you have any queries regarding the contents of this circular, please contact your case officer.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u7.1479"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u10.1587","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Intermediaries Division","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u10.1587"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u12.1614","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"Securities and Futures Commission","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u12.1614"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u13.1649","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"End","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u13.1649"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u14.1654","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"SFO/IS/042/2025","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u14.1654"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"1 As set out in Part III of Schedule 10 to the Code of Conduct for Persons Licensed by or Registered with the Securities and Futures Commission (Code of Conduct).","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u17.1837","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"2 Regulation (EU) 2024/2987 https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/2987/oj/eng","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u17.1837"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u19.1919","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"3 PS23/25 – Margin requirements for non-centrally cleared derivatives: Amendments to BTS 2016/2251 https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/prudential-regulation/publication/2025/november/margin-requirements-for-non-centrally-cleared-derivatives-policy-statement","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u19.1919"},{"locator":"d802c45a4262c.u21.2176","normative":true,"span":null,"text":"4 Binding Technical Standards 2016/2251 refer to the UK version of Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2016/2251 of 4 October 2016 and the regulatory technical standards for risk-mitigation techniques for over-the-counter (OTC) derivative contracts not cleared by a central counterparty.","unit_id":"d802c45a4262c.u21.2176"}]},"task":"REFINE"},"configuration":"ignore-user-config; read-only; tools-disabled; no-resume","events_jsonl":"{\"type\":\"thread.started\",\"thread_id\":\"01a0d865-0a1b-7e30-bf35-ddae4a0074cf\"}\n{\"type\":\"turn.started\"}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_0\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"coverage\\\": [\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted as the announced SFC exemption, its instrument definition, addressed population and duration.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted the original commencement and alignment rationale; insignificant exposures describe the policy rationale, without establishing an individual eligibility threshold.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u1.381\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"EU background: monitoring and periodic reporting qualify the described EU exemption, without express incorporation into the SFC exemption.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u3.801\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"UK background: indefinite duration describes the UK exemption and does not replace the SFC until-further-notice limitation.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u4.1019\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Interpreted as announced future amendment and gazettal; their independent legal significance remains unresolved.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u6.1357\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Provides a contact route for queries, without making consultation or case-officer approval an exemption condition.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u7.1479\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Issuing division identification.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u10.1587\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Issuing authority identification.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u12.1614\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Document end marker.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u13.1649\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Document reference identifier.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u14.1654\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Identifies the margin regime to which the exemption attaches; the incorporated provisions are unavailable.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"INTERPRETED\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Citation supporting EU background; referenced authority contents are not supplied.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u17.1837\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Citation supporting UK background; referenced policy statement contents are not supplied.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u19.1919\\\"},\\n    {\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Defines the technical standards referenced in the UK background, without incorporating them into SFC eligibility.\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"CONTEXT\\\",\\\"unit_id\\\":\\\"d802c45a4262c.u21.2176\\\"}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"dimensions\\\": [\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The circular addresses licensed corporations. Classification and underlying transaction, counterparty and requirement scope depend on the unavailable Code provisions.\\\",\\\"source_unit_ids\\\":[\\\"d802c45a4262c.u0.0\\\",\\\"d802c45a4262c.u15.1671\\\"],\\\"status\\\":\\\"AMBIGUOUS\\\"},\\n    {\\\"dimension\\\":\\\"definitions\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The collective definition covers non-centrally cleared single-stock, equity basket and equity index options. The UK technical-standards definition serves overseas